The port covers the *decode-side* SBR tool only (bitstream parsing,
frequency-band derivation, HF generation/adjustment, and the 32/64-band
QMF analysis/synthesis filterbanks): `oxideav-aac`'s SBR *encoder* and
bitstream *writer* modules were not ported and are not part of this
crate. Parametric Stereo (HE-AAC v2, Annex 8.A) was also not ported;
see `src/aac/sbr/mod.rs` for the integration hook left for that wave.

Every file under `src/aac/sbr/` other than `bits.rs`, `crc.rs`,
`error.rs`, and `mod.rs` (which are small local adapters written for
this port — see their own header comments) is a mechanical adaptation
of the correspondingly-named `oxideav-aac` 0.1.7 source file (e.g.
`src/aac/sbr/header.rs` from `oxideav-aac`'s `src/sbr_header.rs`):
`oxideav_core::bits::BitReader`/`BitWriter` calls were retargeted at
this crate's local `bits` adapter, `crate::{Error, Result}` was
retargeted at a local `error` module reusing the same enum variant
names, and `crate::sbr_<name>::` paths were rewritten to `super::
<name>::`, but the ported logic, structure, item names, and doc
comments (including their spec citations) are otherwise unchanged.

